    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently test the phase state of Earth's core: the Outer Core is liquid while the Inner Core is solid.",
        "The Asthenosphere is explicitly identified as the primary source of magma for volcanic eruptions.",
        "Distinguish carefully between mechanical layers (Lithosphere, Asthenosphere) and compositional layers (Crust, Mantle, Core)."
      ],
      "id": "lqe2fl5"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Based on physical properties, Earth's interior is divided into the Lithosphere, Asthenosphere, Mesosphere, Outer Core, and Inner Core.",
        "The Lithosphere is the rigid, brittle outer layer comprising the crust and uppermost mantle.",
        "The Asthenosphere is a plastic, weak layer in the upper mantle that allows tectonic plates to move.",
        "The Outer Core is liquid and drives Earth's geodynamo, generating the planet's magnetic field.",
        "The Inner Core remains solid despite extremely high temperatures due to overwhelming pressure."
      ],
      "id": "jgkhv9x"
